AlumniConnect database migrations
=================================

Development uses SQLite. Production is prepared for PostgreSQL through the
installed pg8000 driver. DATABASE_URL selects the database; never place real
credentials in this file.

Safe examples:

    DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./alumni.db
    DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME

Run Alembic from the backend directory:

    .\venv\Scripts\alembic.exe current
    .\venv\Scripts\alembic.exe heads
    .\venv\Scripts\alembic.exe history
    .\venv\Scripts\alembic.exe upgrade head

The production application does not create tables automatically. Apply
Alembic migrations explicitly before starting it.

Development/demo data transfer is an explicit operation provided by:

    python scripts/migrate_sqlite_to_postgres.py --dry-run

The utility reads SOURCE_DATABASE_URL and TARGET_DATABASE_URL. Review a dry
run before executing without --dry-run. Never point it at a production target
without explicit authorization and a verified backup/restore plan.
